{
  "title": "Three seeds end with no engine game_end in BOTH schema-eval arms; the XMage AI's search timeout is present but NOT sufficient -- the pilot seat is required",
  "description": "OBSERVED: the schema eval (jobs 9970 guarded, 9972 unguarded, 200 mirror-paired games each) \
banked 185/200 per arm with exactly 15 `launch exited` casualties each. 5 of those are the SAME game \
indices in both arms -- 122, 123, 135, 162, 163 -- collapsing onto three seeds because 122/123 and \
162/163 are mirror pairs: 1200062 and 1200068 (both Ad Nauseam mirrors: JD Nir's Ad Nauseam; Rodrigo \
Togores's Ad Nauseam Tendrils) and 1200082 (Brandon Remley's KikiPod). By chance ~1 overlap is expected \
(15x15/200). The treatment is irrelevant: it fails in both arms and both seatings. In every one the \
launcher printed a clean cost summary, errors.log reads 'No errors detected', and the engine never wrote \
game_end -- the no-signature shape. \
WHAT THE LOGS SHOW: for 1200062 and 1200068 the XMage AI's own detector fired -- ComputerPlayer6 \
`task.get(maxSeconds)` timed out, logging 'AI player thinks too long (report it to github)' and a freeze \
chain, followed within 25-50 s by the launch exiting with no game_end (for 1200062 the timeout is the \
server's LAST log line). 1200062 froze at TURN 2 with 2 permanents and an empty stack; 1200068 at turn 12 \
with a fetchland on the stack. 1200082 shows NO timeout and died while the pilot was mid-MCP call. \
WHAT IS REFUTED, which is the finding: (1) An AI search timeout is NOT sufficient to kill a game. Across \
the vs-engine corpora 31 games ENDED despite one, and all 50 no-game_end games there had NO timeout. \
(2) An engine-vs-engine replay of 1200062 (job 10081, ranokau, eval's own tree wt-schema, skill 1, same \
seed and deck, the XMage AI kept in seat 2) REACHED game_end in 255 s despite TEN timeouts, whose chains \
now name the cards: Scalding Tarn (fetch), Cabal Therapy, Lion's Eye Diamond, Infernal Tutor -- library \
searches and branching choices. The deck reliably explodes the search; the engine survives it. (3) The \
replay did NOT reproduce the eval's state: with an engine in seat 1 instead of the pilot, the board \
diverged from turn 1, and the first timeout came at turn 33, not turn 2. (4) It is NOT the census's h2h \
no-signature bucket: 4452 was head-to-head with no AI seat, so this detector cannot fire there, and none \
of its 200 games shows it. \
CONCLUSION, stated at its real strength: the deaths REQUIRE THE PILOT SEAT. The AI timeout is present on \
two of three seeds and absent on the third; the common factor is the pilot/bridge side, and 1200082 died \
mid-MCP call. Most likely candidates, NOT tested: the pilot's MCP call blocking while the engine is \
stuck, and the harness's idle/launch timeout firing before a game_end is written. \
NEXT STEP: replay 1200062 WITH the pilot in seat 1 (one GPU, 2 games) with DEBUG on mage.player.ai -- \
the shipped log4j.properties holds that package at WARN, which is why the eval shows only the timeout \
line. A pass-through exists in the wt-timing scaffolding tree only. \
ALSO NOTED: MAGEBENCH_AI_RECORD_DIR was set for 10081 and the property is passed by game_processes.py, \
but AiDecisionRecorder wrote nothing -- cause not determined, so the recorder cannot currently be relied \
on for this diagnosis. \
HANDLING IN THE EVAL: these five games are EXCLUDED from the resume (schema_eval_complement \
--exclude-games) and never counted as banked, so the readout reports 195/200, not 200.",
  "correction_2026_09_22": "ROOT CAUSE FOUND for the two Ad Nauseam seeds, and the candidates named \
above were BOTH WRONG -- it is neither an MCP call blocking nor a launch/idle timeout. Found from the \
existing eval logs with no GPU, by lining up the pilot's own timestamps: in every one of the 6 games \
(1200062 g122/g123 and 1200068 g135, both arms) the PILOT PROCESS CRASHED -- run.log reads \
\"[ERROR] Pilot 'Eval122' exited with code 1 -- aborting game\", 13-14 s after its last choose_action \
had SUCCEEDED -- on pilot_rendering.py:591 render_context: \"AssertionError: append-only prompt ~185841 \
tokens exceeds 141312 (serving ceiling 143360 minus 2048 reserved for the completion)\". The transcript \
outgrew the served context (181k-186k tokens across the six) and the harness, correctly, refuses to \
head-truncate an append-only prompt. That one cause explains every property previously attributed \
elsewhere: engine-vs-engine completes because there is no pilot and so no context budget; it is \
deterministic in both arms because transcript length depends on the deal, not the treatment; and \
errors.log reads 'No errors detected' because the assertion fires in the PILOT process while errors.log \
watches only the SERVER -- which is the no-signature shape, explained. The AI's 'thinks too long' timeout \
is a CORRELATE, not a cause: the same combo deck that bloats the transcript also explodes the search. \
STILL OPEN: 1200082 (KikiPod) shows NO overflow assertion and is a different cause. And across all 30 \
casualties in the two arms, only 7 are context overflows; 20 have NO pilot traceback at all, and 3 a \
different exception -- the true no-signature class is the majority and is not explained by this. \
CONSEQUENCE BEYOND THIS EVAL: under MAGEBENCH_CONTEXT_LIMIT=143360 in full-context (append-only) mode, any \
deal whose transcript exceeds ~141k tokens can never reach game_end. That is a structural ceiling on game \
length, deck-dependent, and it silently removes long games from every eval that samples those decks. \
The pilot-seat GPU replay named above is no longer needed for the Ad Nauseam seeds.",
